<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How HBA (Hamza Bashir Marketing Agency) collects, uses and protects information, including data accessed through the Google Ads API."
  updated="November 19, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how HBA (Hamza Bashir Marketing Agency, "we", "us") handles information
    when you visit <a href="https://hamzabashir.pk/">hamzabashir.pk</a>, contact us, or work with us as a client.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details you give us</strong>, such as your name, email, phone/WhatsApp number and business details when you book a call or message us.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising account data</strong> for clients who grant us access to their ad accounts (for example Google Ads, Meta, TikTok), such as campaign, ad group, ad, spend and conversion metrics.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic technical data</strong> such as browser type and pages visited, collected by our hosting provider for security and performance.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Google Ads data and Google user data</h2>
  <p>
    We use an internal tool that connects to the Google Ads API through Google OAuth. It is used only by our own team,
    to read reporting data (campaigns, ad groups, ads, spend and conversions) for Google Ads accounts our clients have asked us to manage.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We request the Google Ads API scope (<code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords</code>) only to read reporting data. The tool does not create, edit or delete campaigns.</li>
    <li>We use this data only to report on and improve the performance of our clients' own advertising.</li>
    <li>We do not sell Google user data, and we do not use it for advertising, profiling or any purpose unrelated to the service.</li>
    <li>We do not share Google user data with third parties, except where required by law.</li>
    <li>Access tokens and reporting data are stored securely and are available only to authorised members of our team.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to enquiries and provide our marketing services.</li>
    <li>To prepare performance reports for our clients.</li>
    <li>To keep our website and systems secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We keep client data only as long as needed to provide our services or as required by law. You can ask us to delete your data,
    or revoke our access to your Google account at any time at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you by emailing us.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>

